  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The narrative is overwhelmingly bullish, driven by an AI-fueled surge in demand for high-capacity NAND flash storage. Persistent supply shortages and disciplined industry capacity have created a favorable pricing environment, particularly for datacenter-grade products. Commentary highlights a structural shift toward long-term agreements with fixed pricing and prepayments, extending revenue visibility well into the future and insulating the company from cyclical volatility. Memory rival Micron’s blowout results further reignited enthusiasm for the sector, positioning Sandisk as a standout beneficiary of the AI infrastructure build-out.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** After spinning off from Western Digital, leadership moved decisively to lock in multi-year customer contracts with prepayment commitments, transforming the business model and boosting cash flow reliability. The company operates with no long-term debt and has generated substantial free cash flow, reflecting disciplined capital allocation. Despite the strong execution, some insider selling at elevated share levels has surfaced as a notable qualitative risk, tempering the otherwise pristine execution story.",
